WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.360
This is pairing buddy:

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:05.060
an AI pair that sits in Neovim,

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.970
and speaks only when it matters.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.430
A test is red,

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.970
and you start fixing the wrong file.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.870
Pair reads the code first,

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.129
then says it right under your line:

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:18.050
the cause is elsewhere.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.550
Alt J jumps there.

00:00:22.398 --> 00:00:24.918
Save, and it runs your tests.

00:00:24.918 --> 00:00:26.838
Your fix broke a queue test?

00:00:26.838 --> 00:00:30.298
Pair says why, and Alt Y takes its fix.

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.488
Or hand it the wheel with Pair drive.

00:00:34.488 --> 00:00:37.608
You watch it type, it tests your unsaved buffer,

00:00:37.608 --> 00:00:39.968
and one undo takes it all away.

00:00:41.678 --> 00:00:43.378
Notes in the margin.

00:00:43.378 --> 00:00:46.158
A first slice from a blank page.

00:00:46.158 --> 00:00:49.838
A ledger of everything it did, and a morning pick-up.

00:00:51.675 --> 00:00:54.375
Any model, local or cloud.

00:00:54.375 --> 00:00:55.555
Pairing buddy:

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.455
the person in the second chair.
